<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	The element order follows the app store schema. The store does not validate
	this file directly, it first runs it through pre-info.xslt and validates the
	result, so unknown elements are dropped silently instead of being rejected.
	There is no element for an app to app dependency, which is why app_api is
	checked at runtime in ExAppService instead of being declared here.
-->
<info>
	<id>findling</id>
	<!--
		The three languages of D-12, and the order is the order of the store
		schema: every name, then every summary, then every description. The
		English wording sits in an element WITHOUT a lang attribute, because
		the schema defaults that attribute to "en"; spelling it out would be a
		second "en" and would break the uniqueness constraint on the element
		kind.

		Not one of these elements may be empty. An empty element in an
		info.xml ends the store upload in a server error rather than in a
		validation message, which is the most expensive known trap of the
		sister project, and the cheapest to walk into while translating.

		The wording is not maintained here. docs/store-listing.md holds all
		three languages of both halves side by side, which is what the
		translation follow up rule of D-12 needs, and
		backend/tests/test_store_metadata.py holds the mechanical part of that
		rule: a language that goes missing from one element kind is a red test.
	-->
	<name>Findling</name>
	<name lang="de">Findling</name>
	<name lang="fr">Findling</name>
	<summary>Zero-config full text, OCR and semantic search for your files</summary>
	<summary lang="de">Volltextsuche, Texterkennung und semantische Suche ohne Konfiguration</summary>
	<summary lang="fr">Recherche plein texte, OCR et recherche sémantique sans configuration</summary>
	<description><![CDATA[What Findling does:
- Full text search in the normal Nextcloud search bar
- OCR for scanned PDFs and images: German, English, French
- Semantic search: finds documents through paraphrases
- Every result is permission-checked by Nextcloud
- No configuration: the first index run starts on its own
- Privacy: everything runs locally, no telemetry, nothing leaves your server

Works together with the [Nextcloud MCP Connector](https://apps.nextcloud.com/apps/mcp_connector): AI assistants receive these search results with exactly the rights of the asking user.

Supported file types:
- PDF (scanned too), DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, ODT, ODS, ODP
- HTML, RTF, TXT, Markdown, CSV
- Images through OCR: JPEG, PNG, TIFF, WebP

Requirements:
- Nextcloud 33 to 35, apps: AppAPI, Findling Backend (External Apps), Findling
- RAM: 4 GB is enough, the container runs under a hard 2 GB limit (measured)
- CPU: 2 cores are enough, amd64 and arm64]]></description>
	<description lang="de"><![CDATA[Was Findling kann:
- Volltextsuche über die normale Nextcloud-Suchleiste
- Texterkennung für gescannte PDFs und Bilder: Deutsch, Englisch, Französisch
- Semantische Suche: findet Dokumente auch über Umschreibungen
- Jeder Treffer wird von Nextcloud rechtegeprüft
- Keine Konfiguration: der erste Indexlauf startet von selbst
- Datenschutz: alles läuft lokal, keine Telemetrie, nichts verlässt den Server

Arbeitet mit dem [Nextcloud MCP Connector](https://apps.nextcloud.com/apps/mcp_connector) zusammen: KI-Assistenten erhalten diese Suchtreffer mit genau den Rechten des fragenden Nutzers.

Unterstützte Dateitypen:
- PDF (auch gescannt), DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, ODT, ODS, ODP
- HTML, RTF, TXT, Markdown, CSV
- Bilder per Texterkennung: JPEG, PNG, TIFF, WebP

Anforderungen:
- Nextcloud 33 bis 35, Apps: AppAPI, Findling Backend (External Apps), Findling
- RAM: 4 GB genügen, der Container läuft unter einer harten 2-GB-Grenze (gemessen)
- CPU: 2 Kerne genügen, amd64 und arm64]]></description>
	<description lang="fr"><![CDATA[Ce que Findling sait faire :
- Recherche plein texte dans la barre de recherche normale de Nextcloud
- Reconnaissance optique pour les PDF numérisés et les images : allemand, anglais, français
- Recherche sémantique : trouve les documents par des périphrases
